JARVIS v8 - INSTALLATION CHECKLIST (Windows 10/11)
====================================================
Follow these steps in order before running jarvis.py.


STEP 0 - BEFORE YOU START
-----------------------------
You need Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit).
Install Python 3.12 from https://www.python.org/downloads/
While installing Python, make sure to check the box that says
"Add python.exe to PATH".
Make sure you have at least 8 GB free RAM (16 GB is better).
Make sure you have at least 10 GB free disk space.
Make sure your microphone and speakers work.
Make sure you are connected to the internet.


STEP 1 - TURN ON MICROPHONE PERMISSIONS
-------------------------------------------
Go to Settings > Privacy & Security > Microphone.
Turn ON "Microphone access".
Turn ON "Let apps access your microphone".
Turn ON "Let desktop apps access your microphone".


STEP 2 - INSTALL OLLAMA (RUNS THE AI LOCALLY)
--------------------------------------------------
Download and install Ollama from https://ollama.com/download/windows
Open a terminal and run these two commands:
      ollama pull qwen3:8b
      ollama pull qwen2.5vl:7b
Keep the Ollama app running in the background the whole time
Jarvis is running. You can check for it in the system tray.


STEP 3 - INSTALL TESSERACT (READS TEXT FROM SCREEN)
---------------------------------------------------------
Open PowerShell and run:
      winget install --exact --id UB-Mannheim.TesseractOCR
Check that it installed to this exact path:
      C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe
Download the Hindi language file from:
      https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata/raw/main/hin.traineddata
Put that file inside:
      C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tessdata\


STEP 4 - INSTALL THE PYTHON PACKAGES
-----------------------------------------
Open the project folder in a terminal and run this command:

python -m pip install customtkinter feedparser mss numpy ollama psutil PyAutoGUI PyAudio pyperclip pytesseract requests screen-brightness-control SpeechRecognition Pillow pywin32 pystray edge-tts

If PyAudio fails to install, run these instead:
      pip install pipwin
      pipwin install pyaudio

After everything installs, check that pywin32 is working by running:
      python -c "import win32com.client; print('pywin32 OK')"
If that gives an error, run:
      python Scripts\pywin32_postinstall.py -install
(the exact path may be different on your PC - look inside your
Python installation's Scripts folder)


STEP 5 - CHECK THAT HINDI VOICE WORKS
------------------------------------------
Open a brand new terminal window and run:
      edge-playback --help
If it says "command not found", do this:
      Find your Python Scripts folder, for example:
          C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python312\Scripts
      Add that folder to your Windows PATH environment variable
      Close and reopen the terminal, then test again


STEP 6 - DOUBLE CHECK EVERYTHING BEFORE RUNNING
-----------------------------------------------------
Make sure the Ollama app is running (look in the system tray).
Run "ollama list" and confirm you see both qwen3:8b and qwen2.5vl:7b.
Confirm Tesseract is at C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe
Confirm microphone permissions are turned on (Step 1).
Confirm all Python packages installed with no errors.


STEP 7 - RUN JARVIS
-------------------------
Run this command:
      python jarvis.py
(use your actual file name if it's different)


IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG
-----------------------------
"I could not connect to Ollama"     -> Ollama isn't running, or the model wasn't pulled
Hindi speech doesn't play            -> edge-playback isn't on PATH, see Step 5
Hindi text not found on screen       -> hin.traineddata is missing, see Step 3
Microphone not detected / silent     -> check Windows privacy settings, see Step 1
PyAudio won't install                -> use pipwin, see Step 4
win32com or SAPI errors              -> run the pywin32 postinstall script, see Step 4
Everything feels really slow         -> your PC may not have enough RAM for the AI models


NOTE ON SHARING THIS WITH OTHERS
--------------------------------------
This assistant will still work fine for anyone, but it currently
says the name "Arsalan" out loud in a few places. If you're giving
this to someone else, you may want to change that name in the code
first.
